Fliplits Privacy Policy
Last updated: October 21, 2026

Fliplits ("the app") is a puzzle game made by Gary Gallagher. This policy explains what information the app handles and why.

Information the app stores
Your game progress (levels, stars, coins, hints, themes and settings) is saved only on your device. We do not run servers that receive this information, and we do not ask you to create an account.

Advertising
The app shows ads provided by Unity Ads (Unity Technologies). To deliver and measure ads, Unity Ads may collect information such as a device advertising identifier, device and network information, approximate location derived from your IP address, and how you interact with ads. Unity's use of this information is described in the Unity Privacy Policy: https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy

The app does not request permission to track you across other companies' apps and websites. If you have not granted tracking permission, ads are not personalised using that identifier. You can limit ad tracking at any time in your device settings.

In-app purchases
Purchases are processed by Apple through the App Store. We never see or store your payment details. Apple shares with the app only what is needed to confirm and restore your purchases.

Children
The app is suitable for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.

Changes
If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted at this address with a new date.

